b(z)=0
Let T be the first time that the chain changes state, \mathbb{E}(Y\mid X_{0}=x)=\mathbb{E}(T\mid X_{0}=x)+\sum\limits_{y\in S}^{}\mathbb{P}\{ X_{t}=y\mid X_{0}=x \}\mathbb{E}(Y\mid X_{0}=y)
This simplifies to \alpha(x)b(x)=1+\sum_{y\neq x,z}^{}\alpha(x,y)b(y)
Say \tilde{\mathbf{A}} is the matrix obtained by deleting the row and column associated with z, then we get \bar{0}=\bar{1}+\tilde{\mathbf{A}}\bar{b}. This is an invertible matrix.
